                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "If you come from a [b] Tactical Ops: Assault on Terror [/b] background it's easy to understand the choices of gunplay etc.\nIf you don't ,    & expected another ordinary shooter game u might find the feel of the game weird and clunky.\n\n\n[h1]PROS [/h1]\n-free to play\n-no microtransaction bs.\n-oldschool game \"remake\"\n-work in progress yet still pretty well executed\n-fun maps (remakes from original game)\n-simular recoil to the original\n-server browser\n\n[h1]KONTRA [/h1]\n-if you come from a cs background (or any other pollished fps) this will feel very clunky to you\n-very basic movement [spoiler] (which is intended & I like it) [/spoiler] but might not be appealing to modern standards\n-clunky menu's / UI very unpollished \n-visibillity of enemy player models weird (light & shading)\n-very little map pool upon this point (22/12/19)\n-keybindings not customizable enough\n\n[spoiler] I love tactical ops where my 3.5 homies @ ? [/spoiler]",
